%% Marquee selection lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no marquee" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No marquee pointer token, anchor, rectangle,
    candidate set, or overlay preview exists.
  end note

  Idle --> DownAdmission: generic pointer session admits down for marquee
  Idle --> Idle: stale move/up/cancel / ignore
  Idle --> Disposed: runtime.dispose()

  state "Down admitted by pointer session" as DownAdmission
  note right of DownAdmission
    Admission is owned by the generic pointer session.
    InteractionEngine records token, session id, anchor,
    controllerEpoch, and previous selection.
  end note

  DownAdmission --> DragPreview: publish zero-area marquee preview / overlay repaint
  DownAdmission --> Idle: invalid down / no preview, edit, or event
  DownAdmission --> Disposed: disposed runtime / StateError

  state "Dragging / overlay-only preview" as DragPreview
  note right of DragPreview
    Move samples normalize the anchor-current rectangle
    and replace CanvasPreviewState. Cleanup and preview
    repaint target the overlay bus only.
  end note

  DragPreview --> DragPreview: same-token finite move / update marqueeRect and overlay repaint
  DragPreview --> DragPreview: stale move, controllerEpoch mismatch, or non-finite move / ignore
  DragPreview --> CandidateQuery: same-token finite up
  DragPreview --> InvalidTerminal: stale, invalid, or non-finite up
  DragPreview --> CleanupOnly: cancel, mode change, interactive=false, load success
  DragPreview --> CleanupOnly: runtime.dispose()
  DragPreview --> DragPreview: load failure / preserve session and preview

  state "Candidate query / read only" as CandidateQuery
  note right of CandidateQuery
    SpatialKernel may be queried only for visible selectable
    marquee candidates whose hitBoundsWorld overlap the
    normalized marquee rectangle. The query cannot mutate
    committed document state or commit selection directly.
  end note

  CandidateQuery --> CandidateQuery: reject stale candidate handle / continue
  CandidateQuery --> SelectionIntent: exact family inclusion and document-order ids
  CandidateQuery --> InvalidTerminal: stale session facts detected

  state "Selection-change intent" as SelectionIntent
  note right of SelectionIntent
    Terminal up computes previousSelection, nextSelection,
    and marqueeRectWorld. This state is only an intent;
    no store/selection-owner mutation or public notification
    has happened.
  end note

  SelectionIntent --> NoOpSelection: next selection empty and previous empty
  SelectionIntent --> NoOpSelection: next selection equals previous selection
  SelectionIntent --> EditCommit: selection changed / open synchronous EditKernel edit

  state "No-op selection cleanup" as NoOpSelection
  note right of NoOpSelection
    Empty-unchanged and unchanged selection paths clear
    marquee preview/session only. They do not open an edit,
    mutate Store, mutate the selection owner, emit an
    action, or publish document/selection state. If an active
    marquee preview is cleared, Runtime publishes CanvasRuntimeState
    with an updated preview revision.
  end note

  NoOpSelection --> CleanupCoordinator: no-op selection cleanup request

  state "EditKernel commit outcome" as EditCommit
  note right of EditCommit
    Selection mutation is committed only through EditKernel
    and the selection owner.
    Atomic install is the commit boundary; rollback or
    rejection leaves selected ids and document/selection state
    unchanged. Active marquee preview cleanup publishes
    CanvasRuntimeState with updated preview revision.
  end note

  EditCommit --> PostCommitCleanup: commit installed with selectionChanged
  EditCommit --> CleanupCoordinator: rollback, rejection, or exception / no action or selection state publication

  state "Post-commit session cleanup" as PostCommitCleanup
  note right of PostCommitCleanup
    Interaction cleanup runs before action events,
    state publication, or repaint signals are
    published to observers.
  end note

  PostCommitCleanup --> CleanupCoordinator: post-success cleanup request

  state "Committed overlay cleanup" as CommittedOverlayCleanup
  CommittedOverlayCleanup --> PublicCommitSignals: overlay cleanup queued and session released

  state "Public state/effects after cleanup" as PublicCommitSignals
  PublicCommitSignals --> Idle: publish CanvasRuntimeState with selection/preview effects, selectMarquee action, main repaint, overlay cleanup repaint

  state "Invalid terminal sample" as InvalidTerminal
  note right of InvalidTerminal
    Stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, invalid session id, non-finite
    terminal facts, and stale candidate generations cannot
    create a commit intent.
  end note

  InvalidTerminal --> CleanupCoordinator: cleanup-only request

  state "Cleanup only" as CleanupOnly
  note left of CleanupOnly
    Cancel, mode change, interactive=false, load success,
    dispose, stale terminal, invalid terminal, no-op, and
    edit failure create typed cleanup requests for marquee
    overlay/session state only.
    Load failure preserves the active marquee when the
    generic pointer session preserves it.
  end note

  CleanupOnly --> CleanupCoordinator: typed cleanup request

  state "PointerToolCleanupCoordinator" as CleanupCoordinator
  note left of CleanupCoordinator
    Coordinator-owned marquee cleanup clears marquee preview
    and session facts and returns an effect-only
    PointerCleanupOutcome. It does not use selected-move
    resolver or main-scene cleanup policy.
  end note

  CleanupCoordinator --> OverlayCleanup: outcome repaint target is overlay
  CleanupCoordinator --> CommittedOverlayCleanup: post-success outcome

  state "Overlay cleanup repaint" as OverlayCleanup
  note right of OverlayCleanup
    Marquee cleanup requests overlay repaint only from the
    coordinator-owned outcome.
    It never uses selected-move resolver, delta staging,
    selected supplement cleanup, or main-scene preview cleanup.
  end note

  OverlayCleanup --> Idle: cleanup finished
  OverlayCleanup --> Disposed: dispose cleanup finished

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  Disposed --> Disposed: later pointer sample or mutating operation / StateError

  note left of DragPreview
    Negative invariants:
    no selected-move resolver, delta, or main-scene preview;
    no direct Store mutation from InteractionEngine;
    no commit on cancel, stale, invalid, or no-op paths;
    no legacy architecture as normative input.
  end note
